r, or that the globs were not altered).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa26ac46261746a24","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope: `criteria_routing.json — tests _comment only, applies_to unchanged`; Acceptance Criteria (no line covers it)","norm_id":"n4c43fbe8eec18818","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor accidentally widens/edits applies_to while adding the _comment and no test catches it","The _comment is left stale/absent"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add a one-line AC asserting the `tests` entry's `applies_to` equals the three existing globs and `_comment` contains the content-trigger description, verified in test_code_review_tests_trigger.py or test_criteria_vocabulary_reviewers.py.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the name-extraction regex skips the optional Go receiver `(...)` (mirroring _REMOVED_DECL_RE at registry.py:402) so the method name — not the receiver token — is compared across added/removed lines in the same file.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.131,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan step 2: 'the name comes from a SEPARATE regex over the matched line, spanning the same keywords (def/class/fn/func/function, const/let/var)'","registry.py:402 `func\\s+(?:\\([^)]*\\)\\s*)?\\w+\\s*\\(` — the matcher already models an optional `(...)` receiver, which the name regex as described does not","Portability AC names 'a Go `func` under `internal/`' as a required SELECT case"],"finding":"The NAME-extraction regex is described as spanning keywords `def/class/fn/func/function, const/let/var` but does not account for the Go receiver form that _REMOVED_DECL_RE already models (`func\\s+(?:\\([^)]*\\)\\s*)?\\w+\\s*\\(`, registry.py:402). For a Go method rename `func (r *T) Old(` → `func (r *T) New(`, a naive first-`\\w+`-after-`func` extraction grabs the receiver token (or empty), not the method name — so the same-file add/remove name comparison that point 4 and the annotation-rewrite negative case rely on can misfire (false trigger, or wrong-name suppression) on Go targets. The portability AC explicitly exercises a Go `func`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcc9d2231974fce64","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 ('the name comes from a SEPARATE regex over the matched line, spanning the same keywords'); AC 'Portability' (Go `func` under `internal/`)","norm_id":"nc32af04bddbfdd48","priority":0.469,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A Go method rename arriving as delete+add where the receiver token is captured instead of the method name","A Go method rename where added and removed method share a receiver but differ in name — name comparison keys off the wrong token"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"ye